## Building cloud-init Configuration

{{ provisioner_name }} serves per-node cloud-init data from its
`metadata-service`, and the compute nodes run the cloud-init client to consume
it. We will establish some basic cloud-init configurations here.

### Create Default Configuration

Let's create a directory to hold our default cloud-init configuration and create
an SSH key pair that we can use for SSH access later.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Create SSH keys -->
```bash
mkdir -p /opt/ohpc/admin/cloud-init
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -q -f "$HOME/.ssh/id_openchami" -N ""
cat >> "$HOME/.ssh/config" <<EOF

Host ${compute_prefix}*
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_openchami
    StrictHostKeyChecking no
    UserKnownHostsFile /dev/null
EOF
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Now we can define the payload to update the defaults.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Create cloud-init payload -->
```bash
cat > /opt/ohpc/admin/cloud-init/defaults.yaml <<EOF
base_url: http://${sms_ip}:8081/metadata-service
cluster_name: CLUSTER
nid_length: 1
public_keys: []
short_name: ${compute_prefix}
EOF
for i in /root/.ssh/id*pub; do
	key=$(cat "$i") yq '.public_keys += [strenv(key)]' \
		-i /opt/ohpc/admin/cloud-init/defaults.yaml
done
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

And then finally upload our payload.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Upload the cloud-init defaults -->
```bash
ochami -k metadata defaults add \
	-f yaml -d @/opt/ohpc/admin/cloud-init/defaults.yaml
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

### Configure Munge

OpenCHAMI's `metadata-service` can be used, in conjunction with the cloud-init
client, to provide post-boot configurations. The configuration below
is a minimal configuration that should at least let the root user login using
the public key and distribute the munge key file to all compute nodes.

The head node answers cloud-init only from privileged source ports (see
[Limiting Access to cloud-init](#limiting-access-to-cloud-init)). The `bootcmd`
below adds the same limit on the compute nodes themselves: only root can reach
ports 8081 and 8443 on the head node.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Cloudinit -->
```bash
munge_key=$(cat /etc/munge/munge.key | base64 -w 0)
export munge_key
sms_addrs="${sms_ip}"
if [[ ${enable_ipoib} -eq 1 ]]; then
	sms_addrs="${sms_addrs}, ${sms_ipoib}"
fi
cat > /opt/ohpc/admin/cloud-init/compute.yaml <<EOF
name: compute
description: compute template
template: |
  ## template: jinja
  #cloud-config
  merge_how:
  - name: list
    settings: [append]
  - name: dict
    settings: [no_replace, recurse_list]
  users:
    - name: root
      ssh_authorized_keys: {% raw %}{{ ds.meta_data.instance_data.v1.public_keys }}{% endraw %}
  bootcmd:
    - |
      nft -f - <<'NFT'
      table inet ohpc {
        chain output {
          type filter hook output priority 0;
          ip daddr { ${sms_addrs} } tcp dport { 8081, 8443 } meta skuid != 0 reject
        }
      }
      NFT
  write_files:
    - content: ${munge_key}
      path: /etc/munge/munge.key
      permissions: '0400'
      owner: munge:munge
      encoding: base64
  runcmd:
    - systemctl restart munge.service
EOF
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Once you are done updating the group you can post the file to the
`metadata-service`.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
```bash
ochami -k metadata group add \
	-f yaml -d @/opt/ohpc/admin/cloud-init/compute.yaml
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
